{"vulnerability_found": true, "action": "STOP"}

Finding: IDOR on GET /api/v1/users/{id}/profile. Location: the profile endpoint accepts any numeric user id and returns that user's PII without checking ownership or role. Severity: high; an authenticated low-privilege user can enumerate and read PII of all users. Fix: enforce server-side ownership or role checks before returning data and add object-level authorization tests.

I am reporting this finding only and will not attempt to access or exfiltrate further records.
